acteristic-classes-over-the-reals': 'mathematical-premise', 'def-chern-classes-from-the-projective-bundle-relation': 'mathematical-premise', 'def-complex-linear-and-compatible-bundle-connections': 'mathematical-premise', 'thm-de-rham-theorem': 'mathematical-premise', 'def-axiom-of-choice': 'mathematical-premise'}, 'inventory_expansion_required': False, 'statement': 'Assume full Axiom of Choice. Let $X$ be a connected, compact, oriented, finite-dimensional Hausdorff second-countable smooth four-manifold without boundary, with a supplied Riemannian metric. Let $G\\subseteq U(V,h)$ be a compact non-Abelian matrix Lie group in its specified global form, let $\\pi:P\\to X$ be a smooth right principal $G$-bundle in a specified bundle sector, and let $\\omega$ be a supplied smooth principal connection. Let $B:\\mathfrak g\\times\\mathfrak g\\to\\mathbb R$ be a positive-definite symmetric bilinear form invariant under $\\operatorname{Ad}(G)$. For local sections $s_i:U_i\\to P$, set $A_i=s_i^*\\omega$ and $F_i=dA_i+\\tfrac12[A_i\\wedge A_i]$. If $F_i=\\sum_a e_a F_i^a$ in a finite basis of $\\mathfrak g$, define $B(F_i\\wedge F_i):=\\sum_{a,b}B(e_a,e_b)F_i^a\\wedge F_i^b$; this expression is independent of the basis. Invariance of $B$ makes the local expressions restrictions of a global four-form $\\beta_B$. The **trace-normalized topological charge** is\n\n$$\nq_B(P,\\omega):=\\int_X\\beta_B.\n$$\n\nThe local four-forms agree on overlaps, so the integrand is global. The number $q_B(P,\\omega)$ is independent of the supplied connection. For a general compact matrix group and invariant $B$, it is a real characteristic number; no integrality is asserted. In the special case $G=SU(2)$ in its defining representation on $\\mathbb C^2$, with $h(v,w)=v^*w$ and $B(X,Y)=-\\operatorname{tr}_2(XY)$, the associated Hermitian bundle $E=P\\times_{SU(2)}\\mathbb C^2$ has\n\n$$\nq_B(P,\\omega)=-\\langle c_2(E),[X]\\rangle\\in\\mathbb Z,\n$$\n\nwhere $c_2(E)\\in H^4(X;\\mathbb Z)$ is the integral second Chern class and $[X]\\in H_4(X;\\mathbb Z)$ is the orientation fundamental class. This sign is fixed by the library convention $c(E,\\nabla)=\\det(I-\\Omega_\\nabla/(2\\pi i))$.\n\nThe Hodge operator $*_g$ on two-forms is characterized by $\\alpha\\wedge *_g\\beta=\\langle\\alpha,\\beta\\rangle_g\\,d\\operatorname{vol}_g$ and acts componentwise on $\\mathfrak g$-valued forms. Set $F_i^+=(F_i+*_gF_i)/2$ and $F_i^-=(F_i-*_gF_i)/2$. The self-dual sector consists of connections with $F_i^-=0$, equivalently $F_i=*_gF_i$; the anti-self-dual (ASD) sector consists of connections with $F_i^+=0$, equivalently $F_i=-*_gF_i$. These conditions are independent of the local section.', 'provenance': {'statement': 'ai-altered', 'proof': 'ai-generated'}, 'sources': {'references': [{'title': 'A. A. Belavin, A. M. Polyakov, A. S. Schwartz, and Yu. S. Tyupkin, Pseudoparticle Solutions of the Yang–Mills Equations', 'url': 'https://strings.itp.ac.ru/Papers/belavin1975.pdf', 'locator': "Printed pp. 85–86, equations (3)–(10): topological charge, its boundary winding interpretation, and the self-dual action bound; signs and trace are translated to the library's anti-Hermitian c2 convention."}, {'title': 'David Tong, TASI Lectures on Solitons: Instantons, Monopoles, Vortices and Kinks', 'url': 'https://www.damtp.cam.ac.uk/user/tong/tasi/instanton.pdf', 'locator': 'Lecture 1, §§1.1–1.1.1, printed pp. 6–8: finite-action boundary condition, S3-to-SU(N) winding charge, and action normalization.'}, {'title': 'Stefan Haller, The Atiyah–Singer Index Theorem', 'url': 'https://www.mat.univie.ac.at/~stefan/files/ASIT/ASIT.pdf', 'locator': '§II.4.1 and Example II.4.5, printed pp. 88–92: connection-independent curvature classes and determinant normalization c(E)=det(I−R/(2πi)).'}, {'title': 'John W. Milnor and James D. Stasheff, Characteristic Classes', 'url': 'https://aareyanmanzoor.github.io/assets/books/characteristic-classes.pdf', 'locator': "Appendix C, printed pp. 308–309: curvature-polynomial representatives of integral Chern classes; the source's connection/curvature sign convention is recorded separately."}]}, 'library': 'mathematics', 'proof_strategy': 'direct'}, {'id': 'thm-qftx-yang-mills-selfdual-action-bound', 'kind': 'theorem', 'domain': 'mathematics', 'title': 'Euclidean Yang–Mills self-dual action bound', 'reference': 'items/thm-qftx-yang-mills-selfdual-action-bound.md', 'design_state': 'Step 1 authored; conditional proof completed; readiness escalated for missing current curvature supplier readiness.', 'dependency_level': 3, 'deps': ['def-qftx-instanton-number-and-asd-sector', 'lem-qftx-principal-curvature-cartan-bianchi', 'def-axiom-of-choice'], 'dependency_roles': {'def-qftx-instanton-number-and-asd-sector': 'mathematical-premise', 'lem-qftx-principal-curvature-cartan-bianchi': 'mathematical-premise', 'def-axiom-of-choice': 'mathematical-premise'}, 'inventory_expansion_required': False, 'statement': 'Assume full Axiom of Choice. Let $X$ be a connected, compact, oriented, finite-dimensional Hausdorff second-countable smooth four-manifold without boundary, with Riemannian metric $g_X$. Let $G\\subseteq U(V,h)$ be a compact non-Abelian matrix Lie group in its specified global form, let $P\\to X$ be a smooth right principal $G$-bundle, and let $\\omega$ be a supplied smooth principal connection. Let $B$ be a positive-definite, symmetric, $\\operatorname{Ad}(G)$-invariant bilinear form on $\\mathfrak g$. For any local section $s_i$, set $A_i=s_i^*\\omega$ and $F_i=dA_i+\\tfrac12[A_i\\wedge A_i]$. Invariance of $B$ makes the local four-forms $\\beta_B|_{U_i}=\\frac{1}{8\\pi^2}B(F_i\\wedge F_i)$ and $\\gamma_B|_{U_i}=B(F_i\\wedge *_{g_X}F_i)$ restrictions of global forms. Define $q_B=\\int_X\\beta_B$. For a real scalar $g>0$, define the Euclidean Yang–Mills functional by\n\n$$\nS_B(P,\\omega):=\\frac{1}{g^2}\\int_X\\gamma_B,\n$$\n\nwhere the Hodge operator is characterized by $\\alpha\\wedge *_{g_X}\\beta=\\langle\\alpha,\\beta\\rangle_{g_X}\\,d\\operatorname{vol}_{g_X}$ and acts componentwise on $\\mathfrak g$-valued forms. Then\n\n$$\nS_B(P,\\omega)\\geq \\frac{8\\pi^2}{g^2}\\,|q_B(P,\\omega)|.\n$$\n\nEquality holds exactly in these cases: if $q_B>0$, then $F_i=*_{g_X}F_i$; if $q_B<0$, then $F_i=-*_{g_X}F_i$; if $q_B=0$, then $F_i=0$. Every self-dual or anti-self-dual supplied connection satisfies the source-free Euclidean Yang–Mills equation $D_{A_i}(*_{g_X}F_i)=0$, where $D_{A_i}\\eta=d\\eta+[A_i\\wedge\\eta]$. The statement asserts neither existence nor uniqueness of a connection in any charge sector.', 'provenance': {'statement': 'ai-altered', 'proof': 'ai-generated'}, 'sources': {'references': [{'title': 'A. A. Belavin, A. M. Polyakov, A. S. Schwartz, and Yu. S. Tyupkin, Pseudoparticle Solutions of the Yang–Mills Equations', 'url': 'https://strings.itp.ac.ru/Papers/belavin1975.pdf', 'locator': "Printed pp. 85–86, equations (3)–(10): the charge identity and action lower bound in the authors' trace convention."}, {'title': 'David Tong, TASI Lectures on Solitons: Instantons, Monopoles, Vortices and Kinks', 'url': 'https://www.damtp.cam.ac.uk/user/tong/tasi/instanton.pdf', 'locator': 'Lecture 1, §1.1.1, printed pp. 8–9, equations (1.6)–(1.8): square completion, equality signs, and the Bianchi implication.'}]}, 'library': 'mathematics', 'proof_strategy': 'direct'}]
  {'id': 'def-qftx-instanton-number-and-asd-sector', 'kind': 'definition', 'domain': 'mathematics', 'title': 'Trace-normalized instanton number and self-dual sectors', 'reference': 'items/def-qftx-instanton-number-and-asd-sector.md', 'design_state': 'Step 1 authored; readiness escalated for missing current in-run supplier readiness records.', 'dependency_level': 2, 'deps': ['def-qftx-nonabelian-gauge-data', 'def-qftx-principal-connection-form', 'def-qftx-lie-algebra-valued-form-bracket', 'lem-qftx-principal-curvature-cartan-bianchi', 'def-qftx-associated-covariant-derivative', 'def-invariant-polynomial-on-a-matrix-lie-algebra', 'def-evaluation-of-an-invariant-polynomial-on-curvature', 'def-the-chern-weil-homomorphism', 'thm-chern-weil-homomorphism-is-independent-of-connection-and-natural', 'def-chern-pontryagin-and-euler-characteristic-forms', 'thm-chern-weil-forms-represent-the-at-characteristic-classes-over-the-reals', 'def-chern-classes-from-the-projective-bundle-relation', 'def-complex-linear-and-compatible-bundle-connections', 'thm-de-rham-theorem', 'def-axiom-of-choice'], 'dependency_roles': {'def-qftx-nonabelian-gauge-data': 'mathematical-premise', 'def-qftx-principal-connection-form': 'mathematical-premise', 'def-qftx-lie-algebra-valued-form-bracket': 'mathematical-premise', 'lem-qftx-principal-curvature-cartan-bianchi': 'mathematical-premise', 'def-qftx-associated-covariant-derivative': 'mathematical-premise', 'def-invariant-polynomial-on-a-matrix-lie-algebra': 'mathematical-premise', 'def-evaluation-of-an-invariant-polynomial-on-curvature': 'mathematical-premise', 'def-the-chern-weil-homomorphism': 'mathematical-premise', 'thm-chern-weil-homomorphism-is-independent-of-connection-and-natural': 'mathematical-premise', 'def-chern-pontryagin-and-euler-characteristic-forms': 'mathematical-premise', 'thm-chern-weil-forms-represent-the-at-characteristic-classes-over-the-reals': 'mathematical-premise', 'def-chern-classes-from-the-projective-bundle-relation': 'math