ibrary convention $c(E,\\nabla)=\\det(I-\\Omega_\\nabla/(2\\pi i))$.\n\nThe Hodge operator $*_g$ on two-forms is characterized by $\\alpha\\wedge *_g\\beta=\\langle\\alpha,\\beta\\rangle_g\\,d\\operatorname{vol}_g$ and acts componentwise on $\\mathfrak g$-valued forms. Set $F_i^+=(F_i+*_gF_i)/2$ and $F_i^-=(F_i-*_gF_i)/2$. The self-dual sector consists of connections with $F_i^-=0$, equivalently $F_i=*_gF_i$; the anti-self-dual (ASD) sector consists of connections with $F_i^+=0$, equivalently $F_i=-*_gF_i$. These conditions are independent of the local section.', 'provenance': {'statement': 'ai-altered', 'proof': 'ai-generated'}, 'sources': {'references': [{'title': 'A. A. Belavin, A. M. Polyakov, A. S. Schwartz, and Yu. S. Tyupkin, Pseudoparticle Solutions of the Yang–Mills Equations', 'url': 'https://strings.itp.ac.ru/Papers/belavin1975.pdf', 'locator': "Printed pp. 85–86, equations (3)–(10): topological charge, its boundary winding interpretation, and the self-dual action bound; signs and trace are translated to the library's anti-Hermitian c2 convention."}, {'title': 'David Tong, TASI Lectures on Solitons: Instantons, Monopoles, Vortices and Kinks', 'url': 'https://www.damtp.cam.ac.uk/user/tong/tasi/instanton.pdf', 'locator': 'Lecture 1, §§1.1–1.1.1, printed pp. 6–8: finite-action boundary condition, S3-to-SU(N) winding charge, and action normalization.'}, {'title': 'Stefan Haller, The Atiyah–Singer Index Theorem', 'url': 'https://www.mat.univie.ac.at/~stefan/files/ASIT/ASIT.pdf', 'locator': '§II.4.1 and Example II.4.5, printed pp. 88–92: connection-independent curvature classes and determinant normalization c(E)=det(I−R/(2πi)).'}, {'title': 'John W. Milnor and James D. Stasheff, Characteristic Classes', 'url': 'https://aareyanmanzoor.github.io/assets/books/characteristic-classes.pdf', 'locator': "Appendix C, printed pp. 308–309: curvature-polynomial representatives of integral Chern classes; the source's connection/curvature sign convention is recorded separately."}]}, 'library': 'mathematics', 'proof_strategy': 'direct'} []
  {'id': 'thm-qftx-yang-mills-selfdual-action-bound', 'kind': 'theorem', 'domain': 'mathematics', 'title': 'Euclidean Yang–Mills self-dual action bound', 'reference': 'items/thm-qftx-yang-mills-selfdual-action-bound.md', 'design_state': 'Step 1 authored; conditional proof completed; readiness escalated for missing current curvature supplier readiness.', 'dependency_level': 3, 'deps': ['def-qftx-instanton-number-and-asd-sector', 'lem-qftx-principal-curvature-cartan-bianchi', 'def-axiom-of-choice'], 'dependency_roles': {'def-qftx-instanton-number-and-asd-sector': 'mathematical-premise', 'lem-qftx-principal-curvature-cartan-bianchi': 'mathematical-premise', 'def-axiom-of-choice': 'mathematical-premise'}, 'inventory_expansion_required': False, 'statement': 'Assume full Axiom of Choice. Let $X$ be a connected, compact, oriented, finite-dimensional Hausdorff second-countable smooth four-manifold without boundary, with Riemannian metric $g_X$. Let $G\\subseteq U(V,h)$ be a compact non-Abelian matrix Lie group in its specified global form, let $P\\to X$ be a smooth right principal $G$-bundle, and let $\\omega$ be a supplied smooth principal connection. Let $B$ be a positive-definite, symmetric, $\\operatorname{Ad}(G)$-invariant bilinear form on $\\mathfrak g$. For any local section $s_i$, set $A_i=s_i^*\\omega$ and $F_i=dA_i+\\tfrac12[A_i\\wedge A_i]$. Invariance of $B$ makes the local four-forms $\\beta_B|_{U_i}=\\frac{1}{8\\pi^2}B(F_i\\wedge F_i)$ and $\\gamma_B|_{U_i}=B(F_i\\wedge *_{g_X}F_i)$ restrictions of global forms. Define $q_B=\\int_X\\beta_B$. For a real scalar $g>0$, define the Euclidean Yang–Mills functional by\n\n$$\nS_B(P,\\omega):=\\frac{1}{g^2}\\int_X\\gamma_B,\n$$\n\nwhere the Hodge operator is characterized by $\\alpha\\wedge *_{g_X}\\beta=\\langle\\alpha,\\beta\\rangle_{g_X}\\,d\\operatorname{vol}_{g_X}$ and acts componentwise on $\\mathfrak g$-valued forms. Then\n\n$$\nS_B(P,\\omega)\\geq \\frac{8\\pi^2}{g^2}\\,|q_B(P,\\omega)|.\n$$\n\nEquality holds exactly in these cases: if $q_B>0$, then $F_i=*_{g_X}F_i$; if $q_B<0$, then $F_i=-*_{g_X}F_i$; if $q_B=0$, then $F_i=0$. Every self-dual or anti-self-dual supplied connection satisfies the source-free Euclidean Yang–Mills equation $D_{A_i}(*_{g_X}F_i)=0$, where $D_{A_i}\\eta=d\\eta+[A_i\\wedge\\eta]$. The statement asserts neither existence nor uniqueness of a connection in any charge sector.', 'provenance': {'statement': 'ai-altered', 'proof': 'ai-generated'}, 'sources': {'references': [{'title': 'A. A. Belavin, A. M. Polyakov, A. S. Schwartz, and Yu. S. Tyupkin, Pseudoparticle Solutions of the Yang–Mills Equations', 'url': 'https://strings.itp.ac.ru/Papers/belavin1975.pdf', 'locator': "Printed pp. 85–86, equations (3)–(10): the charge identity and action lower bound in the authors' trace convention."}, {'title': 'David Tong, TASI Lectures on Solitons: Instantons, Monopoles, Vortices and Kinks', 'url': 'https://www.damtp.cam.ac.uk/user/tong/tasi/instanton.pdf', 'locator': 'Lecture 1, §1.1.1, printed pp. 8–9, equations (1.6)–(1.8): square completion, equality signs, and the Bianchi implication.'}]}, 'library': 'mathematics', 'proof_strategy': 'direct'} []
qftx-instanton-topology-mathematics-examples requires= ['qftx-instanton-topology-mathematics'] items= [{'id': 'ex-qftx-su2-bpst-one-instanton', 'kind': 'example', 'domain': 'mathematics', 'title': 'Charge-one BPST instanton on the round four-sphere', 'reference': 'items/ex-qftx-su2-bpst-one-instanton.md', 'design_state': 'Step 1 authored; conditional global construction completed; readiness escalated for missing current in-run supplier readiness records.', 'dependency_level': 4, 'deps': ['def-qftx-nonabelian-gauge-data', 'def-qftx-principal-connection-form', 'def-qftx-lie-algebra-valued-form-bracket', 'lem-qftx-principal-curvature-cartan-bianchi', 'def-qftx-instanton-number-and-asd-sector', 'thm-qftx-yang-mills-selfdual-action-bound', 'ex-unitary-and-special-unitary-lie-groups', 'thm-heine-borel-rn', 'def-axiom-of-choice'], 'dependency_roles': {'def-qftx-nonabelian-gauge-data': 'mathematical-premise', 'def-qftx-principal-connection-form': 'mathematical-premise', 'def-qftx-lie-algebra-valued-form-bracket': 'mathematical-premise', 'lem-qftx-principal-curvature-cartan-bianchi': 'mathematical-premise', 'def-qftx-instanton-number-and-asd-sector': 'mathematical-premise', 'thm-qftx-yang-mills-selfdual-action-bound': 'mathematical-premise', 'ex-unitary-and-special-unitary-lie-groups': 'mathematical-premise', 'thm-heine-borel-rn': 'mathematical-premise', 'def-axiom-of-choice': 'mathematical-premise'}, 'inventory_expansion_required': False, 'statement': 'Assume full Axiom of Choice. Let $S^4=\\{z\\in\\mathbb R^5:|z|=1\\}$ have its unit round metric. Denote by $p_\\infty$ the point omitted by the north stereographic chart and by $p_0$ the point with north-chart coordinates $x=0$. Orient $S^4$ so that north-chart coordinates $x=(x^1,x^2,x^3,x^4)$ satisfy $dx^1\\wedge dx^2\\wedge dx^3\\wedge dx^4>0$. Set $r^2=\\sum_{\\mu=1}^4(x^\\mu)^2$. The metric in the north chart is $4(1+r^2)^{-2}\\sum_{\\mu=1}^4(dx^\\mu)^2$. Let $U_N=S^4\\setminus\\{p_\\infty\\}$ carry coordinate $x$, and $U_S=S^4\\setminus\\{p_0\\}$ carry coordinate $y=x/r^2$; the metric in the south chart is $4(1+|y|^2)^{-2}\\sum_{\\mu=1}^4(dy^\\mu)^2$.\n\nDefine $SU(2)=\\{U\\in M_2(\\mathbb C):U^*U=I,\\det U=1\\}$. Write $\\epsilon_{123}=1$ and let\n\n$$\n\\sigma_1=\\begin{pmatrix}0&1\\\\1&0\\end{pmatrix},\\qquad\n\\sigma_2=\\begin{pmatrix}0&-i\\\\i&0\\end{pmatrix},\\qquad\n\\sigma_3=\\begin{pmatrix}1&0\\\\0&-1\\end{pmatrix},\\qquad\nT_a=-\\frac{i}{2}\\sigma_a.\n$$\n\nThe $T_a$ are traceless anti-Hermitian generators. Set $B(X,Y)=-\\operatorname{tr}_2(XY)$. Define antisymmetric symbols by $\\eta_{aij}=\\epsilon_{aij}$, $\\eta_{ai4}=\\delta_{ai}$, $\\bar\\eta_{aij}=-\\epsilon_{aij}$, and $\\bar\\eta_{ai4}=\\delta_{ai}$ for spatial indices $i,j\\in\\{1,2,3\\}$, where $\\delta_{ai}$ is the Kronecker delta; extend them antisymmetrically in the last two indices. For a scale parameter $\\rho>0$, define $u(x)=(x^4I-i x^j\\sigma_j)/r\\in SU(2)$ on $U_N\\cap U_S$. Glue the trivial right $SU(2)$-bundles on $U_N$ and $U_S$ by the local-section transition $s_S=s_Nu^{-1}$, and define their local connection potentials by\n\n$$\nA_N=\\frac{2\\eta_{a\\mu\\nu}x^\\nu}{r^2+\\rho^2}T_a\\,dx^\\mu,\\qquad\nA_S=-\\frac{2\\rho^2\\bar\\eta_{a\\mu\\nu}y^\\nu}{1+\\rho^2|y|^2}T_a\\,dy^\\mu.\n$$\n\nOn the overlap these obey $A_S=\\operatorname{Ad}_u A_N+u\\,d(u^{-1})$, so they define a smooth principal connection on the glued bundle. Let $F$ be its global curvature, with chart representatives $F_N$ and $F_S$. In the north chart its curvature, written $F_N=\\tfrac12F^N_{\\mu\\nu}dx^\\mu\\wedge dx^\\nu$, has components\n\n$$\nF^N_{\\mu\\nu}=-\\frac{4\\rho^2}{(r^2+\\rho^2)^2}\\eta_{a\\mu\\nu}T_a.\n$$\n\nLet $*_X$ be the Hodge star characterized on two-forms by $\\alpha\\wedge *_X\\beta=\\langle\\alpha,\\beta\\rangle_X\\,d\\operatorname{vol}_X$, acting componentwise on the Lie-algebra coefficients. This curvature is self-dual, meaning $F_N=*_XF_N$. With $B$ as fixed above, define the charge by $q_B=(8\\pi^2)^{-1}\\int_{S^4}B(F\\wedge F)$ and, for any real $g>0$, define the action by $S_B(g)=g^{-2}\\int_{S^4}B(F\\wedge *_XF)$. Then $q_B=1$, $S_B(g)=8\\pi^2/g^2<\\infty$, and the action saturates the self-dual bound. This is one explicit Belavin–Polyakov–Schwartz–Tyupkin (BPST) charge-one connection; no uniqueness or moduli classification is asserted.', 'provenance': {'statement': 'literature-derived', 'proof': 'ai-generated'}, 'sources': {'references': [{'title': 'A. A. Belavin, A. M. Polyakov, A. S. Schwartz, and Yu. S. Tyupkin, Pseudoparticle Solutions of the Yang–Mills Equations', 'url': 'https://strings.itp.ac.ru/Papers/belavin1975.pdf', 'locator': 'Printed pp. 85–87, equations (3)–(18): charge, self-dual bound, regular finite-action SU(2) charge-one field, and its gauge form.'}, {'title': 'David Tong, TASI Lectures on Solitons: Instantons, Monopoles, Vortices and Kinks', 'url': 'https://www.damtp.cam.ac.uk/user/tong/tasi/instanton.pdf', 'locator': "Lecture 1, §§1.1–1.1.2, printed pp. 6–10, equations (1.1)–(1.11): action and charge conventions, Bianchi consequence, and the charge-one SU(2) connection with 't Hooft symbols."}]}, 'library': 'mathematics', 'proof_strategy': 'direct'}]
