        "statement": "Assume AC. Let \\(T=(\\mathbb R/\\mathbb Z)^r\\) act smoothly on a compact finite-dimensional Hausdorff second-countable manifold \\(M\\) without boundary, let \\(F=M^T\\), and use the product Milnor Borel construction with coefficients \\(k\\in\\{\\mathbb Q,\\mathbb R\\}\\). Let \\(\\mathscr S_T(k)\\) be the multiplicative set generated by the first Chern classes of all nontrivial smooth characters of \\(T\\). Then\n\\[\n\\mathscr S_T(k)^{-1}H_T^*(M\\setminus F;k)=0.\n\\]\nEquivalently, every class in the Borel equivariant cohomology of the nonfixed locus is annihilated by some finite product of nontrivial character classes.",
